     "page": 1,
     "text": "**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Ramsey Potter and Potter Clinic**\n\n**Patient: William Adams** \n**DOB: 04/10/1961** \n**Sex: M** \n**MRN: 771097**\n\n---\n\n**Encounters:**\n\n**2024-11-16:** \n- **Reason for Visit:** Depression / anxiety \n- **BP:** 139/80 \n- **Weight:** 160 lbs\n\n**2024-08-15:** \n- **Reason for Visit:** Depression / anxiety \n- **BP:** 146/73 \n- **Weight:** 165 lbs\n\n**2024-05-13:** \n- **Reason for Visit:** Depression / anxiety \n- **BP:** 147/83 \n- **Weight:** 168 lbs\n\n**2024-02-09:** \n- **Reason for Visit:** Depression / anxiety \n- **BP:** 137/80 **Weight:** 171 lbs\n\n**2023-11-07:** \n- **Reason for Visit:** Depression / anxiety \n- **BP:** 139/85 \n- **Weight:** 172 lbs\n\n**2023-08-05:** \n- **Reason for Visit:** Ankle sprain \n- **BP:** 152/78 \n- **Weight:** 163 lbs\n\n**2023-05-03:** \n- for Visit:** Depression / anxiety \n- **BP:** 152/85 \n- **Weight:** 164 lbs\n\n**2023-01-29:** \n- **Reason for Visit:** Depression / anxiety \n- **BP:** 148/84 \n- **Weight:** 163 **Depression / anxiety (diagnosed 1.7 years ago; 1 medication; controlled; no medications currently prescribed)** \n - Patient presents with ongoing management of his depressive and anxiety symptoms. Despite the chronic nature of his condition, Mr. Adams has been consistently engaged in therapy and reports feeling his symptoms are controlled. No medication has been prescribed as part of his treatment plan at this time. Regular follow-up is recommended to monitor his mental health status and make adjustments to the treatment plan as necessary.\n\n• **Social History:** \n - **Tobacco Use:** Mr. Adams reports smoking cigars approximately four times a month. He started this habit in June 2015 and has not attempted to quit. \n - Consumption:** He consumes approximately eight alcoholic drinks per week. \n\n• **Vital Signs Summary:** \n - **Blood Pressure:** The patient’s blood pressure has been consistently within the range of 137/80 to 152/85 across the recorded visits. \n - **Weight:** His weight has fluctuated between 160 and 172 lbs over the past year, with a general trend towards a slight decrease over time.\n\n• **Past Medical History:** \n - **Ankle Sprain:** In August 2023, Mr. Adams presented with an ankle sprain, which was managed conservatively. He reported no further issues related to this incident in subsequent visits.\n\n• **Family History:** \n - Mr. Adams’s father had hypertension and passed away at the age of 66. There is no reported history of hospitalization for psychiatric conditions in the family.\n\n• **Additional"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "Findings:** \n - Physical examination and routine lab tests have consistently shown no abnormalities. Minor complaints such as occasional headaches and fatigue have been noted but are not considered significant in the context of his primary diagnoses.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** \nMr. William Adams has been under my care for depressive and anxiety disorders, diagnosed approximately 1.7 years ago. His condition is currently controlled without the need for medication. His vital signs are stable, and his weight has shown slight variability. He maintains a habit of smoking cigars and drinks alcohol approximately eight times a week. His recent ankle sprain has fully resolved. Regular follow-up is advised to ensure continued management of his mental health condition.\n"
